+**What the tree holds.** ΚΑΜΨΙΣ T-475: the Cayley Laplacian of `Cay(G, S)` IS the Casimir of the single link, and the "gap" ΚΑΜΨΙΣ reads is its algebraic connectivity. ΑΠΕΡΑΝΤΟΝ's design ladder `Q₈ (t = 3), 2T (5), 2O (7), 2I (11)` with the binary dihedral family at `t = 3` for every `n`.
