+
+§7 left one reading: CMP 95's ellipticity bound, transferred to CMP 109's symmetric averaging. It needs no reading (ledger §109 bis).
+
+THE CURL CONTRACTION. In four dimensions every contour average of Bałaban's form contracts the curl norm, ‖dQA‖² ≤ ‖dA‖², each
+side in its own lattice units. Around a coarse plaquette the radial contour averages cancel at each relative position u, by
+translation covariance. What is left is the average over u of the flux through a fine square of side L. Convexity and
+Cauchy–Schwarz bound its square by L² times that square's plaquette sum, and each fine plaquette lies in exactly L² of the squares.
+The factor is L^{4−d}: four dimensions is exactly where the free action is scale invariant. The k-step average is a composition of
+contractions.
+
+Hence ⟨B, Δ_kB⟩ = min{‖dA‖² : Q^kA = B} ≥ ‖dB‖² — the ellipticity with γ₀ = 1, for every k and for the model of record's averaging.
