(spokes `a, b, c, d` in cyclic order, the pairs not alternating): `Σ_{m,n} tr(σ^m σ^m σ^n σ^n) = 9·2 = 18`; two walls CROSSING (alternating, `a, c, b, d`): `Σ_{m,n} tr(σ^m σ^n σ^m σ^n) = 3·2 − 6·2 = −6`, since `σ^m σ^n σ^m = σ^n` at `m = n` and `−σ^n` at `m ≠ n`. The reference for two walls at one vertex is the product of their single-wall factors over the bare vertex, `6·6/2 = 18`. Hence `φ(touching) = 18/18 = 1` and `φ(crossing) = −6/18 = −1/3`, and by (i) `r = I(S ∪ walls)/I(S) = (−1/3)^{crossings}` for any number of lone walls on any orientable rest, every single wall contributing 1 (its four vertex factors and four link factors multiply to 1 — the identity 16.61 measured on 5,006 chambers and 16.62 on 68 torus rests, now the normalisation of (ii)). The torus derivation of 16.62 (f) is the same number by the other road. **(iv) THREE WALLS AT ONE VERTEX, PREDICTED.** With `Σ_m σ^m A σ^m = 2 tr(A)·1 − A`: the alternating triple (`a, b, c, a, b, c`) gives `Σ_{m,n,p} tr(σ^m σ^n σ^p σ^m σ^n σ^p) = Σ_{n,p} [2 tr(σ^n σ^p)² − tr(σ^n σ^p σ^n σ^p)] = 24 + 6 = 30` against the reference `2·(6/2)³ = 54`: `φ = 5/9`, NOT the pairwise `(−1/3)³ = −1/27`. So the pairwise crossing law holds at vertices carrying at most two walls, and a TRIPLE POINT carries its own Pauli trace: `5/9` for the alternating pattern, and for the other 6-spoke patterns their own traces (`(a, b, c, c, b, a)`: `Σ tr(σ^m σ^n σ^p σ^p σ^n σ^m) = 54`, `φ = 1`; `(a, b, a, c, b, c)`: two crossings sharing a wall, `Σ tr(σ^m σ^n σ^m σ^p σ^n σ^p) = Σ_{n,p} tr((2 tr(σ^n) − σ^n) σ^p σ^n σ^p) = −Σ tr(σ^n σ^p σ^n σ^p) = 6`, `φ = 1/9 = (−1/3)²`). STAKED: the `F = 20` column's `!=` lines, if any, are exactly the chambers with three walls at one vertex, and read `5/9` or `1/9` or `1` per the pattern; a `!=` at a vertex with two walls refutes (iii). **(v) WHAT IS NEW.** Rank-one locality and the Clebsch–Gordan identification are classical (the strong-coupling expansion's vertex factors; W = 0); the law `r = (−1/3)^{crossings}` for lone walls on orientable surfaces, the touching factor 1, the triple-point factors, and their standing as exact pricing in a convergent gas for `SU(2)` on `ℤ⁴` are III's. S8a and S8b (III-Yang_Mills cc85ad7) are theorems for lone walls on orientable rests by (iii); S8c is answered: `−1/3` per crossing, `1` per touching, triple points by their trace.
