+**18.1 THE OBJECT.** In the character expansion of `SU(2)` Wilson theory every plaquette carries a spin `j_p` with weight `d_j a_j χ_j(U_p)`, and the Haar integral over a link variable `U_ℓ` of `Π_{p ∋ ℓ} χ_{j_p}` is the dimension of the invariants of `⊗_{p∋ℓ} V_{j_p}`. The centre `{±1}` acts on `V_j` by `(−1)^{2j}`, so **the integral vanishes unless `Σ_{p ∋ ℓ} 2j_p` is even at every link: GAUSS'S LAW MODULO THE CENTRE** — the N-ality (the centre charge of the flux through the link) is conserved. [W = 0: the centre selection rule is classical ('t Hooft 1978 for the N-ality of flux; the character-expansion form in Drouffe–Zuber 1983).] Consequently every polymer of 16.57's gas is an N-ality assignment: **the half-integer plaquettes form a `Z₂`-cycle — THE LEAF is the world-sheet of N-ality-one (centre-charged, confining) flux — and the integer-spin decorations (walls, pieces, patches) carry N-ality zero (adjoint, centre-neutral, screened).** This is the object: **the centre-charged flux sheet** — the `Z₂`-cycle through `p₀` read as the world-sheet of one unit of centre flux — with its centre-neutral dressing and, at its self-contacts, its exchange channels (18.2). Everything below is a statement about it.
