+**18.6 THE RESOLUTION ROAD: S12 AS A SIGNED SUM OVER THE SHEET'S RESOLUTIONS, THE EXCHANGE SUM KILLED BY GAUGE AVERAGING, AND THE ONE LEMMA LEFT (19:4x EDT; instruments `g56_resolve.pl` 0c987367…, `g57_abstract.pl` 3e5d27cb…, `g58_pinch.pl` 4e64ebb8…, `g59_system.pl` d778f321…; records `g56_f18_leaves.2026-10-29a.txt` b8037384…, `g56_f20_leaves.2026-10-29a.txt` 6dd97f52…, `g57_abstract.2026-10-29a.txt` 385a69cd…, `g58_pinch_{cube,box113,block222}.2026-10-29a.txt` 5dc6d056… 7a312fa3… 7f5d919b… and `g58_pinch_box113.2026-10-29b.txt` e9b0bdaf…, `g59_system_{cube,box113,block222}.2026-10-29a.txt` 0bfa74a0… f3c3ed84… 79344114…; the sets `set_cube.set` `set_box113.set` `set_block222.set` `set_twospheres16.set` `set_torus16.set` `set_leaf18_1.set`; the listings `g50_list_f18_34_0_1.2026-10-29a.txt` and `g50_list_f20_36_0_2.2026-10-29a.txt` by `g50_w64b.exe`, the engine's `W_LISTPROF` extended to even polymers).** (a) THE FORMULA. At a contact link the Haar projector on four spin-½ strands is `(1/6)(|a⟩⟨a| + |b⟩⟨b| + |c⟩⟨c|)` over the THREE pairings (Gram `[[4,2],[2,4]]` in any two, `c = b − a`), so `Z(X) = (2/3)[Z(X_a) + Z(X_b) + Z(X_c)]` for the three complexes with that link resolved; iterating over the `L` contact links and reading a closed sheet at `(−2)^χ` (the crosscap sign, `(−1)^χ` on non-orientable sheets — RP² −2, Klein bottle +1, sphere 4, torus 1): **`Z(X) = (2/3)^L Σ_{x∈{a,b,c}^L} (−2)^{χ(Σ_x)}`**, the sum over all `3^L` resolutions of the sheet. MACHINE-TRUE by an enumerator sharing no line with the engine (a set's sides, links, the `3^L` pairings, union-find on corners for `V`, `χ = V − E + F`): the cube 4, the flat torus 1, the two cubes sharing a square 162 → 32 (the engine's 32; the unsigned sum would read 50.96, so the sign is confirmed in situ: 36 spheres, 24 RP², 12 Klein bottles, 6 tori, 3 disconnected), all 576 contact leaves at `F = 18` (sum 6, Z = 4), and at `F = 20` all 960 two-contact leaves (sum 9 = (3/2)²·4, Z = 4), 3,833 listed single-contact