le-covers the cycle, parallel or doubled, and the disc-swap resolution disconnects; the transfer count confirms `Z/4 = fix(monodromy) − 1 ∈ {0, 2}`); but it is not the whole proof: three minimal pinches admit NO such system and read `Z = 4` all the same (records `g59_system_*`). (d) THE PROOF'S SHAPE. Write the Haar delta at each contact link as `Σ_j d_j χ_j`; only `j ∈ {0, 1}` survive at a sheet edge; so **`Z(X) = 4 + Σ_{∅≠J⊆L} 3^{|J|} 2^F I_J`**, `I_J` the integral over the SHEET with every edge variable independent of `Π_f χ_½ · Π_{ℓ∈J} χ₁(U_{e_ℓ}U_{e'_ℓ}⁻¹)`. THE GAUGE-AVERAGING LEMMA (proved): the plaquette words are invariant under gauge transformations at the sheet vertices; a bridge becomes `χ₁(U_e h U_{e'}⁻¹ k)`, `h = g_{t(e)}⁻¹g_{t(e')}`, `k = g_{h(e')}⁻¹g_{h(e)}`; averaging, `I_J = 0` whenever some sheet vertex enters exactly ONE such ratio — i.e. whenever some FIBRE GRAPH `F_u(J)` (the sheet vertices over a lattice vertex `u`, one edge per link of `J` at `u` joining the two sheet vertices its edges end at, a loop when they coincide, dropped) has a vertex of degree one. A plain leaf of `Ĝ_J` is the special case where the word itself cancels `e e⁻¹`. Hence **`Z(X) − 4` is a sum over the `J` whose every fibre graph is leafless.** THE FIBRE-LEAF LEMMA, measured and half-proved: for a Z₂-minimal `X` with a sphere resolution, every nonempty `J` has a fibre leaf. MEASURED: on all 448 minimal pinches of the three spheres (records `g59_system_*`) no `J` is fibre-leafless — and no `J` is even plainly leafless. PROVED when some partner-closed sub-collection `J′ ⊆ J` has every sheet-vertex degree even (the Eulerian case): a proper two-colouring of the sphere's regions across `Ĝ_{J′}` then exists, cross-pairing by colour at `J′` glues white to white and black to black, the sheet disconnects, minimality fails — this is the σ-cycle theorem in general form and settles every `J` with two links (two columns of equal parity pattern are equal over F₂), every union of cycles